EXPLANATIONS

What is a server:
A device or program that provides functionality to clients over a network.

Role of the domain name:
Provides a human-readable address (www.foobar.com) that maps to the server IP (8.8.8.8), so users dont need to remember IPs.

DNS record type of www:
A record — points www.foobar.com directly to IP 8.8.8.8.

Role of the web server (Nginx):
Receives HTTP/HTTPS requests from the user, serves static content, and forwards dynamic requests to the application server.

Role of the application server:
Executes the application logic, processes dynamic requests, interacts with the database, and returns the result to the web server.

Role of the database (MySQL):
Stores and organizes the application data so it can be read, written, and managed by the application server.

Communication protocol:
The server communicates with the users computer using TCP/IP over HTTP or HTTPS.

---

ISSUES

SPOF (Single Point of Failure):
Only one server — if it goes down, the entire website is unavailable.

Downtime during maintenance:
Deploying new code requires restarting Nginx or the app server, causing temporary unavailability.

Cannot scale:
One server cannot handle a massive spike in traffic — no horizontal scaling possible.
